<title>FRANCE: Irish EU Presidency to talk to Danes about Cuba plan.</title>
<headline>Irish EU Presidency to talk to Danes about Cuba plan.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Irish EU Presidency said on Wednesday it envisaged talks with Denmark about its opposition to European Union efforts to fight Washington's anti-Cuba trade laws.</p>
<p>&quot;We will have to listen and discuss with the Danes even before Monday's (General Affairs Council) meeting,&quot; Irish Foreign Minister Dick Spring told a news briefing at the European Parliament.</p>
<p>EU foreign ministers are due next Monday to discuss laws to block the Helms-Burton Act, an amalgamation of decades of anti-Cuba policy.</p>
<p>Spring said it was important to follow through discussions held at the previous two meetings of EU foreign ministers.</p>
<p>&quot;I will try to reach a conclusion,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Diplomats said on Tuesday Denmark was opposed to EU blocking tactics because it brought into question aspects of national sovereignty.</p>
</text>
